[E0304] Error: cannot assign to `seen`, which this closure only reads
   ╭─[ err/173_iterator_adapters/main.wip:9:9 ]
   │
 9 │         seen += 1
   │         ──┬─
   │           ╰─── captured to read
   │
   │ Help: write the lambda where a `&var (…) => R` is taken, or take what changes as a `&var` parameter of it
   │
   │ Note: a closure lent as `&(…) => R` reads what it captures; one that changes it is a `&var (…) => R`, lent for the call it is written in, or kept in a `val` it is the whole value of
───╯
[E0301] Error: an owned closure is written here, and a lent one is expected
    ╭─[ err/173_iterator_adapters/main.wip:14:48 ]
    │
 14 │ fn owned(text: str): i64 = text.split(" ").map(own (w) => w.len()).count()
    │                                                ─────────┬────────
    │                                                         ╰────────── an owned closure
    │
    │ Help: leave out `own`, so the lambda is lent
    │
    │ Note: `own (x) => …` allocates an environment that holds what it captured
────╯
